# .gitattributes — normalise line endings and protect binary test fixtures.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# The repository stores text blobs with LF line endings, but Git's
# core.autocrlf default on Windows rewrites line endings on checkout. Without
# the rules below that quietly breaks two kinds of test fixtures:
#
#   1. Binary fixtures that contain no NUL bytes. Our simple .pdf fixtures are
#      "text-ish" enough that Git classifies them as text and injects carriage
#      returns on checkout. Those extra bytes shift the PDF's cross-reference
#      (xref) byte offsets, so the pure-Go PDF parser then fails with
#      "malformed PDF: cross-reference table not found". (The .docx/.pptx/.xlsx
#      fixtures escape this only because ZIP archives contain NUL bytes and Git
#      already treats them as binary; marking them here makes that explicit.)
#   2. Text fixtures whose exact bytes are asserted by round-trip / golden
#      tests (for example the CSV round-trip), which break when committed LF
#      line endings become CRLF on a Windows checkout.
#
# Result: every checkout matches the LF blobs already committed, so builds and
# tests behave identically on developer laptops and the Linux CI runners.

# Default: let Git detect text files and normalise them to LF in the repository.
* text=auto

# Binary fixtures — never apply end-of-line conversion (it corrupts bytes).
*.pdf  binary
*.docx binary
*.pptx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.gif  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary

# Text test fixtures whose exact bytes matter must be checked out with LF on
# every platform (not just normalised to LF in the repo).
testdata/*.csv text eol=lf
testdata/*.md  text eol=lf
testdata/*.txt text eol=lf
